#version 460
// THE SCREEN-PROBE GATHER, JOB 3 OF 4: THE FILTER IN PROBE SPACE, AND THE SH
// (PHOTON-GATHER-1b items 2 and 3; SPECS/photon/C2_GATHER_FILTERED_DEFAULT_ON_
// DESIGN.md sections 1.2 and 1.3).
//
// ONE WORKGROUP PER PROBE, one THREAD per texel of its octahedral map — the
// trace's own shape, dispatched from the same indirect arguments.
//
// 1. THE FILTER. Sixty-four rays per probe are a noisy estimate of the
//    radiance arriving at it; the probes around it traced sixty-four more of
//    nearly the same function. Each texel of this probe takes the radiance its
//    3x3 NEIGHBOURHOOD of uniform probes saw IN THE SAME WORLD DIRECTION (the
//    direction re-expressed in each neighbour's own tangent frame and looked up
//    in its map — two probes with different normals hold a direction at
//    different texels), weighted twice:
//      * by PLANE agreement — the neighbour's position against this probe's
//        plane and the two normals, the integrate's own test and tolerances
//        (jahPlaneWeight): a neighbour on another surface saw another
//        hemisphere and says nothing about this one;
//      * by PARALLAX, per texel (ENGINE-POLISH-PHOTON-2 stage 3; Lumen's spatial
//        filter) — a neighbour's ray in the same direction left from ANOTHER
//        point, so the radiance it carries leaves its hit point, which this
//        probe sees in another direction: near an emitter the neighbour's ray
//        meets the panel elsewhere (or not at all) and passed any test of the
//        hit DISTANCE alone. The weight is the ANGLE ERROR of the neighbour's
//        hit point as seen from this probe against the texel's own cone (the
//        closed form at kParallaxOut): full inside the cone, none at twice its
//        half-angle. A hit far away has no parallax, a hit across an occluder
//        between the two probes a large one. A miss is at infinity: two misses
//        agree, a miss never agrees with a hit (whatever the ray's length).
//        THE MISS RULE IS SYMMETRIC ON PURPOSE, and that is what keeps the
//        filter unbiased: a weight that depended on which of the two rays hit
//        (accepting a neighbour's miss beside this probe's hit but rejecting its
//        nearer hit beside this probe's miss, say) is a weight correlated with
//        the radiance, and it darkened the analytic gate's emitter by 7-31 % in
//        the lane's A/B. A hit and a miss beside each other are two surfaces
//        here, never averaged — the noise of a light's edge is the pixel
//        history's to remove (rq_probe_integrate.comp).
//    THE REACH (GATHER-NOISE-1, p.knobs4.z, the arm "gather.filterRadius"): 1,
//    the 3 x 3. Reach 2 (plus the ring of eight at two cells, 17 taps, each
//    under the same two tests) is the measuring arm: it cut the moving floor's
//    noise but BLURRED the walls' lamp gradients — their error against a
//    converged reference +50 %, their mean +0.7 % (gi.flythrough_noise's walls)
//    — and costs 0.14-0.32 ms. With the trace's cross-probe strata
//    (rq_probe_gather.comp) the 3 x 3 taps of one direction are stratified
//    samples of the texel, not independent ones.
//    THE AGE FILTER IS GONE (ENGINE-POLISH-PHOTON-2; U5 decision 21's measuring door): with the
//    parallax test and the grid's jitter the plane fixture reads within its 5 % at two and three
//    strides with the constant width, and the width by the probe's age cost the young pixels' noise
//    bar (gi.gather_estimator 0.825 against 0.80; 0.589 without it).
//    The probe's own texel always weighs 1. An ADAPTIVE probe filters against
//    its CELL's neighbours (its own cell's uniform probe fails its plane by
//    construction — that is why it was appended). The nine taps are read in
//    ONE FIXED ORDER, so the filtered map is a pure function of the atlas:
//    deterministic by construction.
//
// 2. THE SH. The filtered map is projected onto the nine real spherical
//    harmonics over WORLD axes with each texel's exact solid angle
//    (jahOctSolidAngle at the texel's centre), convolved with the clamped
//    cosine and divided by pi, and written into the probe's record — so the
//    integrate evaluates E/pi at the PIXEL's own normal (a pixel's normal is
//    not its probe's) with nine multiply-adds per channel. The projection is
//    normalised per band by the map's own solid-angle sums, and its DC
//    coefficient is then ANCHORED so the SH at the probe's own normal equals
//    GATHER-1a's exact ratio estimator there (the anchor's note below: SH9 is
//    a band-limited kernel, 6-12 % off a rectangular emitter's closed form on
//    its own). The hemisphere under the probe's plane is ZERO in the projection — nothing traced it — which the SH carries as
//    an irradiance that falls off with the tilt away from the probe's normal
//    (exactly (1 + cos t)/2 of a uniform sky), and which the integrate's normal
//    test keeps small (at most 25 degrees).
//    The 64 partial sums are reduced by a FIXED-ORDER shared-memory tree —
//    never an atomic or a subgroup op, whose order is the scheduler's.
//
// 3. THE PREFILTERED MAPS (PHOTON-7 stage 7, 7-3; the lead's ruling B: THE SPLIT
//    SUM ON THE PROBES). The filtered map convolved with the GGX lobe at
//    p.roughLevels' roughnesses, texel by texel, under the split sum's own
//    assumption n = v = r (the convolution HlmsPbs's environment cube holds in
//    its mips): output texel o, direction d_o, takes
//        P(d_o) = SUM_t L_t D(h) (d_o . d_t) dOmega_t / SUM_t D(h) (d_o . d_t) dOmega_t,
//    h the half vector of d_o and d_t - the importance sampler's weight NoL over
//    a pdf of D / 4 with v = n, written as a quadrature over the map's own
//    texels (D's constant alpha^2 / pi cancels in the ratio, so the weight is
//    NoL / ( NoH^2 ( alpha^2 - 1 ) + 1 )^2 with NoH^2 = ( 1 + d_o . d_t ) / 2).
//    The hemisphere holds no texel below the probe's horizon: a lobe near it is
//    renormalised over the texels it has. A texel with no sample weighs nothing
//    (its probe is NO SAMPLE as a whole, below, and no reader takes it). The
//    integrate's ROUGH SPECULAR reads these maps along the lobe's dominant
//    direction (rq_probe_integrate.comp). R11G11B10, one layer a level, at the
//    raw atlas' addressing.
//
// WHAT IT WRITES: the record's SH and its E/pi at the probe's own normal, and the
// prefiltered maps.
#extension GL_GOOGLE_include_directive : require

layout( local_size_x = 8, local_size_y = 8, local_size_z = 1 ) in;

#define JAH_PROBE_PARAMS_BINDING 0
#include "jah_probe_params.glsl"

layout( std430, set = 0, binding = 1 ) buffer Records { JahProbeRecord r[]; } records;
layout( rgba16f, set = 0, binding = 2 ) uniform readonly image2D probeAtlas;
/// THE EYE'S DEPTH (PHOTON-2 stage 2's tail): the 3 x 3 taps' depth walk (jah_probe_seen.glsl).
layout( set = 0, binding = 3 ) uniform sampler2DArray sceneDepth;
/// THE PREFILTERED MAPS (PHOTON-7 stage 7, 7-3; the header's job 3): one layer a roughness level.
layout( r11f_g11f_b10f, set = 0, binding = 4 ) uniform writeonly image2DArray prefilteredAtlas;
#include "jah_reproject.glsl"
#include "jah_probe_seen.glsl"


/// Eight vec4 of partial sums per lane: 27 SH floats (coefficient k, channel c
/// at 3k + c), the cosine-weighted solid angle in the 28th, and in row 7 the
/// plain solid angle (x) and the cosine-weighted radiance (yzw) — the exact
/// quadrature at the probe's own normal that anchors the SH.
shared vec4 gSum[8][64];

/// THE TAP TABLE (fix round, audit F3): the eight neighbours' per-probe facts —
/// the tangent frame (T, B, N in xyz), the plane weight against this probe (T.w;
/// 0 = no tap) and the atlas block (B.w, N.w as floats) — computed ONCE per
/// workgroup by eight lanes, instead of by all 64 lanes nine times over (every
/// lane fetched nine records and rebuilt nine frames). Same arithmetic, same
/// fixed order: the filtered map is bit-identical.
/// Lanes 8..15 fill the SECOND RING (the eight cells at two cells' offset)
/// when the filter's reach is 2 (p.knobs4.z, GatherTuning::filterRadius).
shared vec4 gTapT[16];
shared vec4 gTapB[16];
shared vec4 gTapN[16];
/// ...and its position (the ray origin its hit distances are measured from), for the parallax test.
shared vec3 gTapP[16];
/// THE PROBE'S TEXELS WITH NO SAMPLE this frame (PHOTON-2 stage 2's tail): any makes the whole probe NO SAMPLE.
shared uint gUnsampled;
/// THE FILTERED MAP, SHARED for the prefilter (7-3): a texel's radiance and its solid angle (0 = no sample), and its
/// world direction.
shared vec4 gTexL[64];
shared vec3 gTexD[64];
/// The most roughness levels the prefilter writes (the image's layers; p.roughLevels.z).
const int kRoughLevelsMax = 3;

/// THE PARALLAX TEST (ENGINE-POLISH-PHOTON-2 stage 3; Lumen's spatial filter): a neighbour's ray in
/// direction d from its position q hit at distance t, so its sample is the radiance leaving the point
/// q + t d - which this probe sees in the direction of (q + t d - p), not along d. Its ANGLE ERROR is
/// the angle between the two, taken at the NEARER of the two rays' distances (t = min of this probe's
/// and the neighbour's: the test is then symmetric, see the taps). The closed form of the threshold: a texel of solid angle W stands for
/// the cone of the same solid angle about its centre direction, half-angle a with
/// 2 pi (1 - cos a) = W, i.e. cos a = 1 - W / (2 pi) (at 8 x 8 over the hemisphere, W = 2 pi / 64 on
/// average: a = acos(1 - 1/64) = 0.177 rad, 10.1 degrees). A neighbour's hit inside the cone (error
/// <= a) samples this texel's own radiance and counts fully; its weight falls linearly to none at 2 a.
const float kParallaxOut = 2.0;

ivec2 blockOf( uint probe )
{
	const int atlasCols = max( int( p.knobs3.z ), 1 );
	return ivec2( int( probe ) % atlasCols, int( probe ) / atlasCols ) * kOctResMax;
}

void main()
{
	const uint probe = gl_WorkGroupID.x;
	const uint lane = gl_LocalInvocationIndex;
	const int octRes = int( clamp( p.knobs2.w, 1.0, float( kOctResMax ) ) );
	const uint rays = uint( octRes * octRes );

	const vec4 posW = records.r[probe].posW;
	const vec4 normalW = records.r[probe].normalW;
	const bool onSurface = posW.w > 0.5;
	const ivec2 block = blockOf( probe );
	const ivec2 texel = ivec2( int( lane ) % octRes, int( lane ) / octRes );

	// The probe's cell, and the grid it sits in (rq_probe_gather.comp's rule:
	// an adaptive probe's record names its cell).
	const ivec2 grid = ivec2( p.resolution.xy );
	const uint uniformProbes = uint( max( p.knobs3.x, 0.0 ) );
	const bool adaptive = probe >= uniformProbes;
	const uint cellIndex = adaptive ? uint( max( normalW.w - 1.0, 0.0 ) ) : probe;
	const ivec2 cell = ivec2( int( cellIndex ) % max( grid.x, 1 ), int( cellIndex ) / max( grid.x, 1 ) );
	if( lane == 0u )
		gUnsampled = 0u;		// (ordered before every lane's count by the tap table's barrier)

	// ---- THE TAP TABLE: lane k (0..7) fills neighbour k, row by row with the
	// centre skipped — the fixed order the taps are summed in; lanes 8..15 the
	// same eight directions at two cells (the filter's reach 2).
	const int taps = p.knobs4.z > 1.5 ? 16 : 8;
	if( lane < uint( taps ) )
	{
		const int kk = int( lane ) & 7;
		const int ring = lane < 8u ? 1 : 2;
		const int k = kk < 4 ? kk : kk + 1;
		const ivec2 nc = cell + ivec2( k % 3 - 1, k / 3 - 1 ) * ring;
		float wPlane = 0.0;
		vec3 nT = vec3( 0.0 ), nB = vec3( 0.0 ), nN = vec3( 0.0, 0.0, 1.0 );
		ivec2 nBlock = ivec2( 0 );
		vec3 nP = vec3( 0.0 );
		// A NEIGHBOUR IN THE SAME EYE ONLY (PHOTON-GA-VR): past an eye's last
		// column the probe LIST continues with the OTHER eye's grid.
		if( onSurface && p.knobs4.z > 0.5 && all( greaterThanEqual( nc, ivec2( 0 ) ) ) &&
			all( lessThan( nc, grid ) ) && jahEyeOfCell( nc.x ) == jahEyeOfCell( cell.x ) )
		{
			const uint nb = uint( nc.y * grid.x + nc.x );
			const vec4 nbPos = records.r[nb].posW;
			if( nbPos.w > 0.5 )
			{
				nN = records.r[nb].normalW.xyz;
				// THE PLANE: the neighbour against THIS probe's plane.
				const JahEye tapEye = jahEyeNow( jahEyeOfCell( cell.x ) );
				wPlane = jahPlaneWeight( posW.xyz, normalW.xyz, nbPos.xyz, nN, jahViewDistanceOf( tapEye, posW.xyz ) );
				// ...AND SEEN ALONG THE SURFACE (PHOTON-2 stage 2's tail; 1.6 B4, DEEP_AUDIT photon-diffuse F13): the
				// depth walk from this probe to the neighbour in the eye's picture - no light through a wall thinner than
				// a probe stride on screen (the plane test alone joins the coplanar floors on its two sides).
				vec2 ownUv;
				float ownZ;
				if( wPlane > 0.0 &&
					( jahReproject( posW.xyz, tapEye.camPos, tapEye.perspective, tapEye.rayTL, tapEye.rayRight,
									tapEye.rayDown, tapEye.fwd, ownUv, ownZ ) != 0 ||
					  !seenAlongSurface( posW.xyz, ownUv, nbPos.xyz, tapEye, jahEyeOfCell( cell.x ),
										 vec2( float( jahEyeWidth() ), p.resolution.w ) ) ) )
					wPlane = 0.0;
				jahTangentFrame( nN, nT, nB );
				nBlock = blockOf( nb );
				nP = nbPos.xyz;
			}
		}
		gTapT[lane] = vec4( nT, wPlane );
		gTapB[lane] = vec4( nB, float( nBlock.x ) );
		gTapN[lane] = vec4( nN, float( nBlock.y ) );
		gTapP[lane] = nP;
	}
	barrier();

	vec3 filtered = vec3( 0.0 );
	vec3 dirW = vec3( 0.0, 0.0, 1.0 );
	float solidAngle = 0.0;
	float cosine = 0.0;
	// THE TEXEL HAS A SAMPLE (PHOTON-2 stage 2's tail, 1.6 A2): a ray whose record a full hit list dropped is NO SAMPLE
	// (kAtlasNoSample, rq_probe_gather.comp) - never a black ray: left out of the filter (a neighbour's tap) and of the
	// SH sums below. AND A PROBE THAT LOST ANY RAY IS NO SAMPLE AS A WHOLE (irradiance.w -1, below): a list overflows
	// at its END, so a probe in flight when it filled loses a WARP of its lanes - a contiguous half of its octahedral
	// map, one side of the hemisphere - and the ratio estimator over the other half is the brighter (or darker) side's
	// mean, not the hemisphere's (measured: photon-room's floor +13 to +26 codes under the overflow arm); its pixels
	// keep their history instead (rq_probe_integrate.comp), exactly as for a probe that lost every ray.
	bool sampled = false;

	if( onSurface && lane < rays )
	{
		const vec3 n = normalW.xyz;
		vec3 T, B;
		jahTangentFrame( n, T, B );
		// THE TEXEL'S CENTRE DIRECTION and its exact solid angle — the
		// quadrature the SH projection integrates with.
		const vec3 octPoint = jahOctPoint( ( vec2( texel ) + 0.5 ) / float( octRes ) );
		const vec3 dLocal = octPoint / max( length( octPoint ), 1e-6 );
		dirW = normalize( T * dLocal.x + B * dLocal.y + n * dLocal.z );
		solidAngle = jahOctSolidAngle( octPoint, float( octRes ) );
		cosine = max( dLocal.z, 0.0 );
		// The texel's cone (the parallax test's closed form, above): cos a = 1 - W / (2 pi).
		const float coneHalf = max( acos( clamp( 1.0 - solidAngle / 6.28318531, -1.0, 1.0 ) ), 1e-4 );

		const vec4 own = imageLoad( probeAtlas, block + texel );
		sampled = !( own.w <= kAtlasNoSample + 0.5 );
		if( !sampled )
			atomicAdd( gUnsampled, 1u );
		vec3 sum = sampled ? own.xyz : vec3( 0.0 );
		float wsum = sampled ? 1.0 : 0.0;

		// (a texel with no sample takes no neighbour either: the parallax test reads its own ray's length)
		if( sampled && p.knobs4.z > 0.5 )
		{
			// THE NINE TAPS, IN ONE FIXED ORDER (row by row); the centre is this
			// probe itself and is already in the sum. The neighbours' frames and
			// plane weights come from the workgroup's tap table.
			for( int k = 0; k < taps; ++k )
			{
				const float wPlane = gTapT[k].w;
				if( wPlane <= 0.0 )
					continue;
				const vec3 nT = gTapT[k].xyz, nB = gTapB[k].xyz, nbN = gTapN[k].xyz;
				// THE SAME WORLD DIRECTION in the neighbour's own frame.
				const vec3 l = vec3( dot( dirW, nT ), dot( dirW, nB ), dot( dirW, nbN ) );
				if( l.z <= 0.0 )
					continue;		// under the neighbour's horizon: it never traced it
				const ivec2 nt = clamp( ivec2( jahOctUv( l ) * float( octRes ) ), ivec2( 0 ),
										ivec2( octRes - 1 ) );
				const vec4 s = imageLoad( probeAtlas,
										  ivec2( int( gTapB[k].w ), int( gTapN[k].w ) ) + nt );
				if( s.w <= kAtlasNoSample + 0.5 )
					continue;		// the neighbour's ray has no sample this frame
				// THE PARALLAX: the neighbour's hit point as this probe sees it.
				// A MISS IS AT INFINITY: two misses agree (no parallax at infinity),
				// a miss and a hit never do (whatever the ray's length happens to be).
				// Two hits are compared at the NEARER of the two distances (Lumen's
				// rule): t = min( this probe's, the neighbour's ). At the neighbour's own
				// distance alone the test is not symmetric: this probe's ray stopped on
				// a pillar at 0.3 m while the neighbour's, 0.2 m aside, passed it to a
				// wall at 10 m reads an angle error of 0.02 rad and the wall's radiance
				// would enter a texel that shows the pillar - and the reverse pair would
				// be rejected, a weight correlated with which ray is occluded. At the
				// nearer distance both orders read the same parallax. The test reads the
				// texel's CENTRE direction dirW, not the direction the neighbour's ray
				// actually took inside its own texel: a sub-texel error inside the cone.
				// A distance that is not finite (an fp16 atlas overflow) weighs nothing.
				float wHit = 0.0;
				if( own.w < 0.0 || s.w < 0.0 )
					wHit = ( own.w < 0.0 && s.w < 0.0 ) ? 1.0 : 0.0;
				else if( finite1( own.w ) && finite1( s.w ) )
				{
					const float t = min( own.w, s.w );
					const vec3 seen = gTapP[k] + dirW * t - posW.xyz;
					const float len = length( seen );
					const float cosErr = len > 1e-6 ? dot( seen, dirW ) / len : 1.0;
					const float err = acos( clamp( cosErr, -1.0, 1.0 ) );
					wHit = finite1( err ) ? clamp( ( kParallaxOut - err / coneHalf ) / ( kParallaxOut - 1.0 ), 0.0, 1.0 )
										  : 0.0;
				}
				const float w = wPlane * wHit;
				if( !( w > 0.0 ) || !finite3( s.xyz ) )
					continue;
				sum += s.xyz * w;
				wsum += w;
			}
		}
		filtered = sampled ? sum / wsum : vec3( 0.0 );
	}

	// ---- THE PREFILTERED MAPS (7-3; the header's job 3) ----------------------
	gTexL[lane] = ( sampled && finite3( filtered ) ) ? vec4( clamp( filtered, vec3( 0.0 ), vec3( 1024.0 ) ), solidAngle )
													 : vec4( 0.0 );
	gTexD[lane] = dirW;
	barrier();
	if( onSurface && lane < rays )
	{
		const int levels = clamp( int( p.roughLevels.z + 0.5 ), 1, kRoughLevelsMax );
		float a2[kRoughLevelsMax];
		vec3 acc[kRoughLevelsMax];
		float wacc[kRoughLevelsMax];
		for( int k = 0; k < kRoughLevelsMax; ++k )
		{
			const float r = p.roughLevels.x + p.roughLevels.y * float( k );
			a2[k] = r * r * r * r;   // alpha = r^2 (perceptual roughness), alpha^2 = r^4
			acc[k] = vec3( 0.0 );
			wacc[k] = 0.0;
		}
		for( uint t = 0u; t < rays; ++t )
		{
			const vec4 Lt = gTexL[t];
			const float c = dot( dirW, gTexD[t] );
			if( !( Lt.w > 0.0 ) || c <= 0.0 )
				continue;
			const float noh2 = 0.5 + 0.5 * c;
			for( int k = 0; k < kRoughLevelsMax; ++k )
			{
				if( k >= levels )
					break;
				const float den = noh2 * ( a2[k] - 1.0 ) + 1.0;
				const float w = c * Lt.w / ( den * den );
				acc[k] += Lt.xyz * w;
				wacc[k] += w;
			}
		}
		for( int k = 0; k < kRoughLevelsMax; ++k )
		{
			if( k >= levels )
				break;
			const vec3 v = wacc[k] > 0.0 ? acc[k] / wacc[k] : vec3( 0.0 );
			imageStore( prefilteredAtlas, ivec3( block + texel, k ), vec4( finite3( v ) ? v : vec3( 0.0 ), 0.0 ) );
		}
		// THE QUADRATURE DOOR (a test door, p.roughLevels.w >= 1): the filtered map itself, in the layer after the levels
		if( p.roughLevels.w > 0.5 )
			imageStore( prefilteredAtlas, ivec3( block + texel, levels ), vec4( gTexL[lane].xyz, 0.0 ) );
	}

	// ---- THE SH PROJECTION, one texel per lane -------------------------------
	float y[9];
	jahShBasis9( dirW, y );
	const float dw = sampled ? solidAngle : 0.0;
	if( !sampled )
		cosine = 0.0;
	float part[28];
	for( int k = 0; k < 9; ++k )
	{
		const float c = y[k] * dw * jahShCosineOverPi( k );
		part[3 * k + 0] = filtered.x * c;
		part[3 * k + 1] = filtered.y * c;
		part[3 * k + 2] = filtered.z * c;
	}
	part[27] = cosine * dw;
	for( int v = 0; v < 7; ++v )
		gSum[v][lane] = vec4( part[4 * v], part[4 * v + 1], part[4 * v + 2], part[4 * v + 3] );
	gSum[7][lane] = vec4( dw, filtered * ( cosine * dw ) );
	// The fixed-order tree: lane k adds lane k+s for s = 32, 16, 8, 4, 2, 1.
	for( uint s = 32u; s > 0u; s >>= 1u )
	{
		barrier();
		if( lane < s )
			for( int v = 0; v < 8; ++v )
				gSum[v][lane] += gSum[v][lane + s];
	}
	barrier();
	if( lane == 0u )
	{
		JahProbeRecord rec = records.r[probe];
		const float cosSum = gSum[6][0].w;
		const float omegaSum = gSum[7][0].x;
		const bool answered = onSurface && cosSum > 1e-6 && omegaSum > 1e-6;
		// THE RATIO ESTIMATOR'S NORMALISATION, per band: over the hemisphere the
		// solid angle is 2 pi and the cosine-weighted solid angle pi, exactly; the
		// quadrature's own sums stand in for them — band 0 by the first, bands 1
		// and 2 by the second — so a UNIFORM environment reads exactly its
		// radiance at the probe's normal whatever the quadrature's error (the
		// uniform hemisphere's band-2 projection is zero).
		const float norm0 = answered ? 6.28318531 / omegaSum : 0.0;
		const float norm12 = answered ? 3.14159265 / cosSum : 0.0;
		for( int v = 0; v < 7; ++v )
		{
			vec4 c = gSum[v][0];
			for( int j = 0; j < 4; ++j )
			{
				const int f = 4 * v + j;		// flat float index; coefficient f / 3
				c[j] *= ( f < 3 ) ? norm0 : norm12;
			}
			if( v == 6 )
				c.w = 0.0;
			if( !( finite3( c.xyz ) && finite1( c.w ) ) )
				c = vec4( 0.0 );
			rec.sh[v] = c;
		}
		// THE ANCHOR. A nine-coefficient SH is a band-limited kernel, not the
		// clamped cosine: evaluated at the probe's own normal it reads a
		// rectangular emitter's irradiance 6-12 % low near it and 6 % high at a
		// grazing distance (spikes/photon-gather-1b, the octahedral quadrature
		// against Lambert's closed form) — where GATHER-1a's quadrature was
		// exact. So the SH carries the VARIATION with the normal and the exact
		// quadrature carries the value: the DC coefficient is moved so that the
		// SH evaluated at the probe's normal IS the ratio estimator's
		//     E/pi = SUM( L cos dOmega ) / SUM( cos dOmega ),
		// and a pixel on the probe's own plane reads that exactly while a tilted
		// one reads it plus the SH's difference (a control variate: the error is
		// the SH's error in the DIFFERENCE, which vanishes with the tilt).
		vec3 e = vec3( 0.0 );
		if( answered )
		{
			const vec3 anchor = gSum[7][0].yzw / cosSum;
			const vec3 band = jahProbeShEval9Raw( rec, normalW.xyz );
			const vec3 dc = ( anchor - band ) / 0.282095;
			rec.sh[0].xyz += dc;
			e = clamp( anchor, vec3( 0.0 ), vec3( 1024.0 ) );
			if( !( finite3( rec.sh[0].xyz ) && finite3( e ) ) )
			{
				for( int v = 0; v < 7; ++v )
					rec.sh[v] = vec4( 0.0 );
				e = vec3( 0.0 );
			}
		}
		records.r[probe].sh = rec.sh;
		// w: 1 answered; -1 NO SAMPLE (on a surface, a ray's record dropped by a full hit list: the integrate's pixels
		// keep their history rather than read a part of the hemisphere or hand the frame to the fallback); 0 no answer.
		const bool noSample = onSurface && gUnsampled > 0u;
		records.r[probe].irradiance = vec4( e, noSample ? -1.0 : answered ? 1.0 : 0.0 );
	}
}
